/*****************************************************************************
    stringT -- the fixture for the `#` string expression (StringXP), 2026-07-31.

        StringXP    "#"- stuff=PrintXP+ defer;

    `#` replaces the old `string` keyword, so a string expression is written
    with the SAME vocabulary as print, shortcuts included, and ExpressioN
    needs no shortcut vocabulary of its own. It was tried as `,` first and
    that collided with the shortcut set -- incant/hashProbe is that record.

    WHAT THIS FIXTURE IS FOR, and it is not "does `#` work once":

    ⚠ IT MUST WORK ON THE SECOND EXECUTION OF THE SAME STATEMENT. An action
    body is parsed once into a cached BlocK and then re-executed (see
    project memory: "Executed BlocK is built once and cached"). So a StringXP
    node is a REUSED node, and anything the action does to that node's own
    term list is permanent. Rows 1 and 2 below are the same source line reached
    twice; row 2 is the one that carries the information.

    THE `$` TOGGLE IS PERSISTENT NOW. `useDefaultSpace = true` was removed from
    opPrint and opString, so `$` toggles and STAYS toggled; processAction sets
    it back to true before each action runs, so it cannot leak INTO an action,
    but it does survive across statements WITHIN one, and a nested action call
    resets it. Rows 3 and 4 pin both halves of that.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT, and it is load-bearing: an incant parse failure
    abandons the rest of the file AND EXITS 0 (CLAUDE.md testing doctrine,
    third corollary). Absent sentinel => the run truncated => every "ok" above
    it is uninterpretable, not merely incomplete.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(StringTest);
define
    /*  One `#` statement, reached twice. Balanced `$...$`: toggle spacing off
        for the join, toggle it back on, so the statement does not depend on
        what ran before it.  */
    mintOne argument code={
        pikkle = #$"bcLabel" argument$;
        print "  mint [" pikkle "]":;
        };

    /*  Persistence WITHIN an action: the first `$` turns spacing off and the
        second statement inherits it, with no `$` of its own.  */
    spanner code={
        first  = #$"aa" "bb";
        second = #"cc" "dd";
        print "  toggle held [" first "][" second "]":;
        };

    runStringT code={
        print "1 first execution":;
        mintOne(1);
        print "2 SECOND execution of the same statement":;
        mintOne(2);
        print "3 default spacing":;
        plain = #"xx" "yy";
        print "  joined [" plain "]":;
        print "4 toggle persists within one action":;
        spanner();
        };
    ;

runStringT();
print "ST SENTINEL":;
stop();
